{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1418923-a-couple-of-questions-on-extended-spellcasting-rolls","id":1418923,"title":"A couple of questions on extended spellcasting rolls","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-18T19:04:30-07:00","id":1418923,"title":"A couple of questions on extended spellcasting rolls","content":"1. When a mage spends Quintessence to reduce the difficulty of his Arete roll, does it apply only to one single roll, or to every roll made during the casting of that one Effect? I had been pretty sure it was the former, but I can't find it clearly stated in the book anywhere.<br /> <br /> 2. The optional rule on M20 p. 541-542 indicates that casting a Great Work takes five hours <i>per roll</i>. Per &quot;Rituals and Stamina&quot; on p. 541, a mage can work on a ritual for <i>one</i> hour per Stamina point before having to start making Stamina rolls <i>each</i> hour (with increasing difficulty each time) or else spend WP to keep going.<br /> <br /> So, realistically even a mage with Stamina 5 is going to have a pretty tough time attempting two Great Work rolls in a row. The good news is that you can take a break from a Great Work...but then you have to spend a WP <i>and</i> make an increasing-difficulty roll for each break. (At least <i>this</i> roll is Attribute+Ability, and you could plausibly refresh some WP in the 48 hours before you have to get back to your Great Work. But still.)<br /> <br /> Am I missing something? Is this actually meant to be as difficult as it seems to be? Are you supposed to be buffing yourself with some kind of Eldritch Caffeine rote in order to keep yourself going through these rituals? If this was a game-balance issue intended to make Effects requiring 10+ successes into genuinely epic feats, making the whole rule optional would be a little bizarre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T04:44:37-07:00","id":1418986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1. When a mage spends Quintessence to reduce the difficulty of his Arete roll, does it apply only to one single roll, or to every roll made during the casting of that one Effect? </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M20.p332</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can spend Quintessence to reduce the difficulty<br /> of <b><u>A</u></b> magick casting roll. Each point spent reduces that<br /> difficulty by 1, to a maximum reduction of -3.</div> </div> </div> </div>It applies to one single roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Am I missing something? Is this actually meant to be as difficult as it seems to be? </div> </div> </div>Probably? It IS the key to &quot;godlike&quot; feats, after all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are you supposed to be buffing yourself with some kind of Eldritch Caffeine rote in order to keep yourself going through these rituals? </div> </div> </div>Most likely. At least if you want to roll more than once each few days. You could also use magick to lower the difficulty ot all the rolls (and I think the rule of -3 it's over the base value, so you could erase any number of penalties - albeit at a certain point you migth end needing a Great Work to do your Great Work if we take this path too far).<br /> You can also increase Stamina past 5, if you don't mind taking risk with &quot;temporary&quot; Permadox (goes away after you loose the dots. I imagine that you will have Quintessence, so pattern bleed doesn't need to be an issue)<br /> <br /> I think *these* rules are meant for people that know the rules, use the rules, and see no shame on using them to their advantage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If this was a game-balance issue intended to make Effects requiring 10+ successes into genuinely epic feats, making the whole rule optional would be a little bizarre. </div> </div> </div>Not really. The game balance issue of rituals being quite OP (depending on how you interpret some rules), was a complaint of many (myself included), but not of everyone. Hence you can opt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-19-2020, 07:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T11:38:56-07:00","id":1419054,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the rules are difficult... but there are ways to deal with it... and those ways are actually good for the setting:<br /> <br /> 1) Great Works are easier to do in Sanctums (high level ones significantly decrease your need to spend Quintessence on difficulty mods) or in the Umbra. Being in a place where buffing yourself to superhuman endurance isn't vulgar is a huge plus.<br /> 2) Great Works are easier to do with a group of mages capable of sharing the same magical style.<br /> 3) Great Works are easier to do with a bunch of acolytes helping sort out the detail.<br /> <br /> So it very much behooves masters to cultivate students that are indoctrinated into their magical style, a community of believers in their paradigm, and to claim/guard special places to do their most powerful magic. Or in other words, there's a really good reason for there being Traditions/Crafts/Conventions instead of every mage just doing their own thing. When you can get -2 difficulty, +5 successes, and +5 dice to each ritual roll... you can see why the book offers some pretty harsh options to keep that in check. You can also see why groups of like-minded mages are as well positioned in the setting compared to ones that focus on individualism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T13:58:32-07:00","id":1419084,"title":"","content":"A fair thing to point out that these harsh rules are unique to M20, so if they feel a bit wonky that's huge reason why. Revised did not have this level of difficulty when it came to such rolls, instead the roll duration was based on the paradigm of the caster and the whims of the GM. In that edition, your greatest concern was accumulating Paradox by botching a roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T19:53:10-07:00","id":1419111,"title":"","content":"Thanks, everyone. I can definitely see why you'd want to make it harder to do huge spells, so that some random PC who gets bored can't spend a day and just set off a 30-success Ball of Abysmal Flame in the location of their choice (presuming adequate Correspondence). On the other hand, even if you reduce the difficulty, making an extended roll with 3-5 Arete dice (assuming you don't have archmage PCs) each time seems pretty hazardous to me already.<br /> <br /> Or maybe that's just because I have terrible luck with d10s.<br /> <br /> I guess the sudden jump to five hours per roll feels a little arbitrary? Or maybe it's just that putting the limit on &quot;number of successes&quot; instead of &quot;number of rolls&quot; feels wrong to me, even though for game balance purposes it probably makes more sense.<br /> <br /> It sort of makes me want to consider alternate ideas for keeping a lid on uber-spells. Has anyone tried anything like that? I was vaguely considering the idea of attaching a Quintessence cost to every roll after the mage had made more than (Arete) rolls, but that probably isn't going to hold many established Mage PCs back for long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T22:07:37-07:00","id":1419125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1418923-a-couple-of-questions-on-extended-spellcasting-rolls#post1418923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Per &quot;Rituals and Stamina&quot; on p. 541, a mage can work on a ritual for one hour per Stamina point before having to start making Stamina rolls each hour (with increasing difficulty each time) or else spend WP to keep going.</div> </div> </div> </div>Outside of ritual, a Mage working an eight hour day at an office and using Magick to accomplish things can keep using Magick and Ability rolls to reduce each other's difficulty. We assume most people can do something for eight hours, as part of the Consensus relating to how labor is organized. Serfs worked 18 hour days for much of the year. Meditative yoga actually gives you more energy. <br /> <br /> With Mind 3, one of the Mages could form a Mind-link with other Mage-participants to permit those with different Foci to join without causing paradox. They could then sleep and carry on the ritual through lucid dreaming, if the ritual was planned in stages where waking and dreaming accomplish different aspects Effect. <br /> <br /> Inventors using Matter, Forces and Correspondence are at a huge disadvantage compared to mystics using Life and Mind. Perhaps why some Iterators want to become robots. Assuming a group has the Spheres, Mind 5, Matter 4, Forces 3, Prime 2, they could put their consciousness into robots and plug into the power grid to forgo Stamina roles.<br /> <br /> Another thing that could influence the ritual's goals: the Nature of each Mage participant. If a goal was envisioned that speaks to each person's Nature, they could regain Willpower from having completed each stage. The desire to do good work and seeing the foundation laid pushes them forward. A Caregiver and a Sadist would have a hard time, unless it was to get justice against a wrongdoer who had escaped prosecution and thereby permit people to heal. The Sadist sees the pain inflicted on the target. The Caregiver observes the relief the victims get from justice done. More compatible Natures: Praise-Seeker and Visionary. &quot;Finally, my vision is manifest. I owe it all to you.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T10:30:37-07:00","id":1419187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1418923-a-couple-of-questions-on-extended-spellcasting-rolls?p=1419125#post1419125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Outside of ritual, a Mage working an eight hour day at an office and using Magick to accomplish things can keep using Magick and Ability rolls to reduce each other's difficulty. We assume most people can do something for eight hours, as part of the Consensus relating to how labor is organized. Serfs worked 18 hour days for much of the year. Meditative yoga actually gives you more energy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of assume that working on a big ritual is meant to be significantly more fatiguing than a normal workday, otherwise the rules as listed don't make any sense at all.<br /> <br /> I dunno. It's hard to get a frame of reference for how difficult will-working actually is ICly. I guess the answer is &quot;pretty damn.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1418923-a-couple-of-questions-on-extended-spellcasting-rolls?p=1419125#post1419125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Mind 3, one of the Mages could form a Mind-link with other Mage-participants to permit those with different Foci to join without causing paradox. They could then sleep and carry on the ritual through lucid dreaming, if the ritual was planned in stages where waking and dreaming accomplish different aspects Effect.<br /> <br /> Inventors using Matter, Forces and Correspondence are at a huge disadvantage compared to mystics using Life and Mind. Perhaps why some Iterators want to become robots. Assuming a group has the Spheres, Mind 5, Matter 4, Forces 3, Prime 2, they could put their consciousness into robots and plug into the power grid to forgo Stamina roles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you actually need the Mind-link thing? M20 p. 542 suggests that mages from different Traditions can work together if they approach each other's practices respectfully and work out some shared cues, although there may be social rolls involved.<br /> <br /> (&quot;Look, I don't care what you call it in Latin. Just draw whatever symbols you need, and then signal me when it's time to inject the phlogiston.&quot;)<br /> <br /> It seems a little weird to imagine mages with wildly different practices doing this, but if they <i>couldn't</i>, people would have a pretty strong incentive to make PC groups all of the same Tradition or something. I doubt most of us really want that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1418923-a-couple-of-questions-on-extended-spellcasting-rolls?p=1419125#post1419125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing that could influence the ritual's goals: the Nature of each Mage participant. If a goal was envisioned that speaks to each person's Nature, they could regain Willpower from having completed each stage. The desire to do good work and seeing the foundation laid pushes them forward. A Caregiver and a Sadist would have a hard time, unless it was to get justice against a wrongdoer who had escaped prosecution and thereby permit people to heal. The Sadist sees the pain inflicted on the target. The Caregiver observes the relief the victims get from justice done. More compatible Natures: Praise-Seeker and Visionary. &quot;Finally, my vision is manifest. I owe it all to you.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to need to review the WP recovery rules, actually. So many WW/OP games with <i>kinda</i> similar rules to keep track of...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T22:31:07-07:00","id":1419305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1418923-a-couple-of-questions-on-extended-spellcasting-rolls?p=1419187#post1419187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of assume that working on a big ritual is meant to be significantly more fatiguing than a normal workday, otherwise the rules as listed don't make any sense at all.<br /> <br /> I dunno. It's hard to get a frame of reference for how difficult will-working actually is ICly. I guess the answer is &quot;pretty damn.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with the ritual mechanic is that it necessitates itself. The opposed the faction's past successful ritual or &quot;project&quot; will mandate the players having to overcome the forty accumulated successes with a ritual of their own. The Technocracy gets to use companies and engineering teams. Mystic Tradition players have to start a cult. Common.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1418923-a-couple-of-questions-on-extended-spellcasting-rolls?p=1419187#post1419187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you actually need the Mind-link thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, definitely not needed. Mind is already overpowered. Making it a requirement for anything else puts less used Spheres to further shame. I believe a Mind-link would facilitate communication a little better, while posing privacy issues. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1418923-a-couple-of-questions-on-extended-spellcasting-rolls?p=1419187#post1419187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to need to review the WP recovery rules, actually. So many WW/OP games with <i>kinda</i> similar rules to keep track of...</div> </div> </div> </div>Something hopefully helpful - an example from my most recent session. I had determined that there was an effect in play over a wide area created by two NPC Mages. One is an ItX -Statistician. The other Syndicate - Media Control. A TV show produced by the Technocracy is used to diffuse the effect. Correspondence 4, Mind 4, Entropy 3, Time 4 - Selecting a possible future the TV show is based on, and then seeding it into the minds of the population to permit some version of that reality to be created, in opposition to current cultural values. Media controversy about the show's message is also used, because the injection of an idea into the Consensus doesn't require positive emotions, only strong ones. The production of a season finale episode is how I imagined the Ritual, benefitting from the sleeper/EC actors' best performances. It takes a few days to shoot an episode, in this case. <br /> <br /> Where I left room for the players to detect and overcome the effect was the tech-Mages' accumulated successes being spent partly on reaching a large audience. The players don't yet have the resources needed to get forty successes. Plus, they are merely at the stage of analyzing the effect. They used Magick facilitating Ability rolls. They did not have all of the Spheres to completely understand the effect, metaphysically. I allowed perception + awareness to give them some clue and to rise above the effect long enough to carry on. They rolled Intel + Research to analyze the message and mundane tricks (actor sex appeal, controversy, outrage) used to insert it into public consciousness. Intel + Science to devise a step by step mundane method to alert small groups of people and train them to spread awareness, advancing critical arguments against the Union's propaganda.<br /> <br /> In an upcoming session, there will be a chance to write a paper, Intel + Academics, bringing social scientists to their side. One character has Merits related to singing and will be able to record music that speaks to the values they are defending, Charisma + Art. As they gather resources and sleeper allies, they can start to plan a &quot;ritual&quot; type event that overcomes the Technocracy's success so far. <br /> <br /> My technocrat NPCs have positioned themselves to ride the counterwave, instead of sending ECs to crash the event. Tradition mages incurring a large amount of paradox is not particularly advantageous to the Union, since it could produce Marauders. There's a story reason why one faction might allow the other to attempt their ritual, if you find it hard to imagine how the players could fortify the location. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}